{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>And the altar shall be holy.</b> And what is its holiness? <b>Whatever touches the altar shall become holy.</b> Even a disqualified offering that went up on it — the altar sanctified it to render it valid so that it not be taken down. From the fact that it says ״כָּל הַנֹּגֵעַ בַּמִּזְבֵּחַ יִקְדָּשׁ,״ I would hear [that this applies] whether fit or unfit — for instance something whose disqualification did not pertain to holiness, such as the sodomizer and the sodomized and מֻקְצֶה and נֶעֱבָד and טְרֵפָה and the like — therefore Scripture says, adjacent after it, ״וְזֶה אֲשֶׁר תַּעֲשֶׂה״: just as the עֹלָה is fit, so too everything that was fit [at the time] it was seen [i.e., accepted] and was then disqualified after it came into the courtyard — such as הַלָּן and הַיּוֹצֵא and הַטָּמֵא and one slaughtered with intent of חוּץ לִזְמַנּוֹ and חוּץ לִמְקוֹמוֹ and the like (Zevaḥim 3)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:55:41.929299266Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}